---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A link button is a native <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> that looks like a button. Use it when activating the
  control navigates; use <a href='/components/button'><code>wc-button</code></a> when it runs an action or
  submits a form. It replaces <code>wc-button href</code>, which is deprecated.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-link-button href='/components/button'>Read the button docs</wc-link-button>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Link attributes</h3>
<p>
  <code>href</code>, <code>target</code>, <code>rel</code> and <code>download</code> pass to the link.
  With <code>target="_blank"</code>, set <code>rel="noopener noreferrer"</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'} inline>
  <wc-link-button href='https://github.com/redvars' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>
    <wc-icon name='open_in_new' slot='icon'></wc-icon>GitHub
  </wc-link-button>
  <wc-link-button href='/favicon.svg' download='peacock.svg' variant='outlined'>Download</wc-link-button>
</DemoComponentCard>
